From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: retry verified present writable PS4 guest faults once

Pass the x86 page-fault error code to the PS4 fault hook. This lets the
platform-specific hook distinguish a present user write protection fault from
an unmapped-page fault before attempting its bounded per-page protection
resynchronization.

---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 29d7c704d2..0000000000 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -3465,10 +3465,12 @@ static void __attribute__((used)) segv_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo,
              * page unmapped while it is replaced with flexible memory. If a
              * guest thread faults on that exact page during the replacement,
              * wait for the mapping operation and retry the instruction only
              * when its requested access is valid in the settled mapping. */
-            extern int __wine_ps5_wait_for_exec_migration( const void *, unsigned int ) __attribute__((weak));
+            extern int __wine_ps5_wait_for_exec_migration( const void *, unsigned int,
+                                                            unsigned int ) __attribute__((weak));
             if (__wine_ps5_wait_for_exec_migration &&
                 __wine_ps5_wait_for_exec_migration( siginfo->si_addr,
-                                                     (unsigned int)rec.ExceptionInformation[0] ))
+                                                     (unsigned int)rec.ExceptionInformation[0],
+                                                     (unsigned int)ERROR_sig(sigcontext) ))
             {
                 leave_handler( data, sigcontext );
                 return;
-- 
